Step A — Test the Go application locally
From the Experiment 10 folder:

go test -v ./...
go run .


curl http://localhost:8080/
curl http://localhost:8080/health
curl http://localhost:8080/metrics

Step B — Test the Docker image

docker build -t devops-go-app:local .

docker run --rm \
  -p 127.0.0.1:8080:8080 \
  devops-go-app:local

#Step C — Prepare Jenkins and Docker Hub
Create a Docker Hub repository named devops-go-app.

In Jenkins, configure a credential with ID dockerhub-credentials and assign the devops-k8s label to a trusted agent with Go, Docker, Git, and kubectl installed.

Configure Kubernetes credentials for that agent. Avoid exposing the Docker socket or Kubernetes administrator credentials to untrusted jobs.



Step D — Configure Jenkins Pipeline
Job name	End-to-End-DevOps
Type	Pipeline
Definition	Pipeline script from SCM
SCM	Git
Branch	*/main
Script Path	Experiment-10-End-to-End-DevOps/Jenkinsfile
DOCKERHUB_USER	Your Docker Hub username


Step E — Install monitoring
After the Jenkins deployment succeeds, run:

chmod +x monitoring_commands.sh
./monitoring_commands.sh


Step F — Access application and monitoring
Use separate terminals for port forwarding:

# Application
kubectl port-forward \
  -n devops-lab \
  svc/devops-go-service 8080:80

# Grafana
kubectl port-forward \
  -n monitoring \
  svc/monitoring-grafana 3000:80

# Prometheus
kubectl port-forward \
  -n monitoring \
  svc/monitoring-kube-prometheus-prometheus 9090:9090
